        "translator": "K. M. K. Murthy / Desiraju Hanumanta Rao",
        "text": "\"On the departure of Bharata, that splendid Rama, truth-bound, and self-controlled, anticipated the repeated visits of citizens and other people. To be undisturbed, Rama then entered Dandaka forests... [1-1-39b, 40]"
